  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: d01fd2d64a9249049aaa77d5c12a82fe, type: 3}
  m_Name: Question 7
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  questionText: "7. Taking a higher concentration of Na2S2O3 solution than KI decreases
    the time taken for the appearance of blue colour in the solution.\t"
  referenceImage: {fileID: 0}
  explanationText: The higher the concentration of Na<sub>2</sub>S<sub>2</sub>O<sub>3</sub>
    solution, the higher the time taken to consume all the sodium thiosulphate solution
    by iodide ions, slowing the formation of the complex with starch, resulting in
    blue colouration, increasing the time taken for the appearance of blue colour
    in the solution.
  options:
  - True
  - False
  correctOptionIndex: 1
